(any) joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by G-7 will be," may determine the JPY/KRW's near-term movement, says Samsung Futures analyst Jeon Seung-ji; she tips near-term support at 13.4000. But she adds, though the issue of political unrest in the Middle East and North Africa has somewhat shifted out of the market focus now, investors should keep an eye on issues in that region as well. The USD/KRW is at 1,129.50. (min-jeong.lee@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0151 GMT [Dow Jones] Thai shares are expected to rise in tandem with healthy gains in most external bourses. "The SET Index should be able to stage a mild rebound after Thursday's fall. However, I don't expect it to go far as worries over Japan's nuclear issue and its impact still (present an) overhang," says BFIT Securities strategist Aphisit Limsupanark. Resistance is pegged at 1015, while support is at 996; shares closed down 0.6% at 1002.35 Thursday. Focus will be on developments at Japan's Fukushima nuclear power plant for trading cues. Heavyweight energy blue chips are expected to lead gains following the rise in global oil prices. (phisanu.phromchanya@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0150 GMT [Dow Jones] China shares are higher, taking their cues from a stronger Nikkei, helped by the G-7 agreeing on joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to pare down yen strength. The Shanghai Composite Index is up 1.0% at 2927.23, and analysts peg immediate resistance at 2950. Still, "uncertainties over possible monetary tightening steps (in China) during the upcoming weekend is likely to cap the upside," says Capital Securities analyst Jacky Zhang. Coal miners are among leading gainers, rising on hopes of higher coal prices on the back of stronger oil prices; \uc2 China Shenhua Energy\uc2  (601088.SH) adds 2.6% to CNY28.80 while Chine Coal Energy (601898.SH) rises 2.4% to CNY11.48. Brokerages advance on bargain buying after yesterday's declines, with Hong Yuan Securities (000562.SZ) up 