\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen falls after G7 deal, further downside seen\b0\par\par\uc2 660 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 01:52\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Yen drops nearly 3 pct vs dollar\par \par \uc2 * G7 agrees on joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , BoJ pumps liquidity\par \par \uc2 * UN resolution on Lybia no-fly zone adds to nerves\par \par \uc2 SYDNEY, March 18 (Reuters) - The yen skidded on Friday after the Group of Seven finance ministers agreed to act to limit the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength, with the dollar popping above 81 yen in a move that could put further pressure on players to unwind long yen positions.\par \par \uc2 Japanese Finance Minister Yoshihiko Noda said Japan agreed with central banks of the United States, Britain and Canada as well as the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to jointly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the first joint action in over a decade.\par \par \uc2 Traders said the Bank of Japan was immediately spotted buying dollars versus the yen, though it seemed to be meeting heavy offers.\par \par \uc2 "Were we to break up 81-81.25, it would certainly mean that the speculators who had been trying to front-run repatriation would feel very very uncomfortable," said Robert Rennie, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Westpac Bank.\par \par \uc2 The dollar jumped nearly 3 percent on the day to as high as 81.48 yen , extending a rebound from a record low of 76.25 yen plumbed on Thursday. The selloff in the previous session came after a break of the 1995 record low of 79.75 triggered a cascade of automatic sell orders in thin trade.\par \par \uc2 The yen has climbed steadily since last week's earthquake, as Japanese and international investors closed long positions in higher-yielding, riskier assets such as the Australian dollar, funded by cheap borrowing in the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Expectations that Japanese insurers and companies will bring money home to pay for claims and reconstruction also contributed to the yen's strength.\par \par \uc2 The euro jumped 2.8 percent to 113.71 yen , while commodity \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , such as the Australian dollar performed even better, having recently been hammered particularly hard.\par \par \uc2 The Aussie surged 3.7 percent to 80.37 yen.\par \par \uc2 WILL \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  BE SUCCESSFUL?\par \par \uc2 Some analysts doubted any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be effective, given past experiences by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is no panacea. Everyone knows it. \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has a much bigger credibility problem and that'll weaken the impact," said David Gilmore, a partner in \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Analytics in Essex, Connecticut.\par \par \uc2 "I don't think we've seen the low in the dollar/yen. There's still a lot of carry trade exposure. The world is really levered up on this."\par \par \uc2 Yet, other analysts said \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be more effective this time than it was in September when Japan spent $26 billion to weaken the yen but failed to ensure a lasting dollar rally.\par \par \uc2 "This entire move can be pinned down to speculative positioning rather than any repatriation flows," said Lee Hardman, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  economist at \uc2 Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Since it is speculative, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in this case should work and clear out some of the long yen positions."\par \par \uc2 The cost of hedging against a further yen rise fell, with implied volatility on one-month dollar/yen trading at around 16 percent, down from near 21 percent on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere, the euro retreated against the dollar, but held near a 2011 high around $1.4053 set overnight after solid demand at a Spanish bond auction.\par \par \uc2 Views that euro zone interest rates were likely to rise soon also helped underpinned the common \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which last stood at $1.3988 .\par \par \uc2 The dollar bounced off a record low of 0.8852 Swiss francs\par \par \uc2 at 0.9086 francs. The franc had benefited from the recent market turmoil as it is usually seen a safe port in a storm.\par \par \uc2 The franc had earlier edged up after the U.N Security Council voted to authorise a no-fly zone over Libya, prompting further gains in oil prices.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Ian Chua in Sydney and Wanfeng Zhou in New York; Editing by Wayne Cole)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110318e73i0001d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
