\par\par \b \uc2 INTERVIEW-UPDATE 1-G7 ready to act again if needed-Japan vice finmin\b0\par\par\uc2 565 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 09:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * G7, Japan ready to act again to counter speculation\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  satisfied with \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 's impact on yen, stocks\par \par \uc2 * BOJ should continue to supply ample funds to maximise impact\par \par \uc2 (Adds more quotes)\par \par \uc2 By Tetsushi Kajimoto and Yuko Noshikawa\par \par \uc2 March 18 (Reuters) - The Group of Seven is ready to "act decisively" again if \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market speculation persists, Japanese deputy finance minister Fumihiko Igarashi said on Friday after the G7 agreed to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  together to restrain the soaring yen.\par \par \uc2 Igarashi told Reuters in an interview he was satisfied with the impact the rare joint action had on Japanese markets, helping boost stocks and weakening the yen.\par \par \uc2 The G7 show of solidarity came as a surprise to many because Tokyo had indicated it was looking for moral support for its attempts to calm markets rather than concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "The yen's rise was driven by speculators," Igarashi, one of Finance Minister Yoshihiko Noda's two deputies, said.\par \par \uc2 "G7 countries agreed that if we caved in to such speculators that took advantage of people's misfortunes, the Japanese economy would be ruined and the whole world economy would be harmed," he said.\par \par \uc2 "Our stance remains unchanged that we will take decisive steps against speculators who act like sneaky thieves at a scene of a fire."\par \par \uc2 G7 agreed that authorities should in principle stay away from markets but that Japan was in a state of emergency, struggling to cope with a triple blow of a deadly earthquake, tsunami and the world's worst nuclear accident since Chernobyl.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar surged two full yen to as much as 81.83 yen\par \par \uc2 , leaving behind a record low of 76.25 hit earlier this week as the Bank of Japan kicked off the joint action. Media reported it bought more than $25 billion.\par \par \uc2 Asked about the size of Friday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Igarashi said he simply was not sure what was the total amount.Japan's Nikkei share index climbed nearly 3 percent, recouping some of the week's stinging losses in the aftermath of last week's 9.0 magnitude earthquake.\par \par \uc2 As he was speaking, traders were reporting that European \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sprung into action, with French and German central banks officially confirming they took part in the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Igarashi said the finance ministry expected the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to continue supplying ample funds to financial institutions to maximise the impact of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "We think it is desirable for the BOJ to steadily carry it out (ample fund injections) and we highly value the fact that the bank has been doing so."\par \par \uc2 Igarashi said much credit for the swift and rare G7 action went to Noda and his good relations with U.S. Treasury Secretary Timothy Geithner, and that it was not certain before Friday's G7 conference call that it would lead to a joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "It was not clear if the statement would turn out this clearcut (on joint action). Noda took strong initiative in seeking a clear stance on this and persuaded other countries to agree."\par \par \uc2 The last time the G7 agreed on joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was a decade ago to turn a slumping euro following its 1999 launch.\par \par \uc2 The G7 comprises Canada, France, Germany, Italy, Japan, the United Kingdom and United States.\par \par \uc2 (Editing by Tomasz Janowski)\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 JAPAN\b0 \highlight\uc2 -ECONOMY/\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (INTERVIEW, UPDATE 1)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110321e73i000fx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
