\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  finmin: joint  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  not targeting specific levels\b0\par\par\uc2 142 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 02:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, March 18 (Reuters) - Japanese Finance Minister Yoshihiko Noda said the G7 was not targeting specific \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels in its joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced on Friday.\par \par \uc2 The joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is basically aimed at dollar/yen, but the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may also \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the euro, he told reporters.\par \par \uc2 Noda also said the Japanese government is not considering asking the Bank of Japan to directly underwrite its debt, saying that cautious debate would be needed on such a move.\par \par \uc2 The Group of Seven advanced nations will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  jointly in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets at the request of the Japanese authorities struggling with the yen's rise and a deepening nuclear crisis, finance chiefs from the group said on Friday.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Tetsushi Kajimoto; Editing by Michael Watson)\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 JAPAN\b0 \highlight\uc2 /\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2 -NODA (URGENT)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110321e73i0002m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
