\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-G7 agrees to joint  \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention \highlight\uc2  to help  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 258 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 01:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Tokyo to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  from 0000GMT, buy dollar/yen - Noda\par \par \uc2 * Noda declines to comment on size of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 (Adds quotes, details)\par \par \uc2 By Leika Kihara and Tetsushi Kajimoto\par \par \uc2 TOKYO, March 18 (Reuters) - The Group of Seven industrial nations agreed on Friday to jointly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to stem a sharp yen rise that complicates Japan's battle with the devastation caused by last week's violent earthquake and an unfolding nuclear crisis.\par \par \uc2 "Given yen moves after the tragic events that hit Japan, the United States, Britain, Canada and the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  have agreed with \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to jointly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market," Finance Minister Yoshihiko Noda told reporters.\par \par \uc2 Japanese authorities will buy dollar/yen in the market from 9 a.m. (0000 GMT). Other central banks will act when their markets open, Noda said. He declined to comment on the size of Tokyo's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "When \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  is in such a state, it's extremely meaningful for G7 countries to cooperate and take coordinated action to stabilise financial markets," he said.\par \par \uc2 The dollar spiked about 2 yen to above 81 yen on Friday, after the news, moving away from a record low against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit earlier this week.\par \par \uc2 Tokyo last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on its own on Sept. 15, 2010, when it sold 2.13 trillion yen, a record amount for a single day.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Tetsushi Kajimoto, Leika Kihara; Editing by Tomasz Janowski)\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 JAPAN\b0 \highlight\uc2 /\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (URGENT) (UPDATE 1)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110321e73i0000p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
