\par\par \b \uc2 TEXT-G7, BOJ statements on  \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 269 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 01:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  TOKYO, March 18 (Reuters) - The Group of Seven industrial nations and the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  issued following statements on their joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2  Statement of G7 Finance Ministers and \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governors, March 18th, 2011:\par \par \uc2  "We, the G7 Finance Ministers and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governors, discussed the recent dramatic events in Japan and were briefed by our Japanese colleagues on the current situation and the economic response put in place by the authorities.\par \par \uc2  We express our solidarity with the Japanese people in these difficult times, our readiness to provide any needed cooperation and our confidence in the resilience if the Japanese economy and financial sector.\par \par \uc2  In response to recent movements in the exchange rate of the yen associated with the tragic events in Japan, and at the request of the Japanese authorities, the authorities of the United States, the United Kingdom, Canada, and the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will join \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , on March 18, 2011, in concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in exchange markets. As we long have stated, excess volatility and disorderly movements in exchange rates have adverse implications for economic and financial stability. We will monitor exchange markets closely and cooperate as appropriate."\par \par \uc2  Statement by the BOJ Governor:\par \par \uc2  "The Bank of Japan strongly expects that Japan's concerted action with G7 member countries in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market will contribute to the stable formation of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates.\par \par \uc2  The Bank of Japan will pursue powerful monetary easing and, to ensure stability in financial markets, will continue to provide ample liquidity."\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Tomasz Janowski)\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 JAPAN\b0 \highlight\uc2 /\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (URGENT) (UPDATE 1)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110321e73i0000o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
