\par\par \b \uc2 Euribor rates up as Japan woes muddy ECB rate plans\b0\par\par\uc2 555 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 11:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 FRANKFURT, March 18 (Reuters) - Key euro-priced bank-to-bank lending rates rose on Friday as debate intensified whether Japan's quake and nuclear troubles could see the ECB delay its rate hike plans following its part in joint G7 \b \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The dramatic events in \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  over the last week have muddied the waters on the ECB's repeatedly flagged plans to rates by 0.25 percent next month. (for analysis click [ID:nLDE72F0VC])\par \par \uc2 G7 members stepped up their efforts to prevent any further escalation in financial market volatiliy on Friday by jointly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to tame the recent sharp rise in the yen. [ID:nL3E7EH3HN]\par \par \uc2 The three-month Euribor rate <EURIBOR3MD=> -- traditionally the main gauge of unsecured interbank euro lending and a mix of interest rate expectations and banks' appetite for lending -- rose to 1.172 percent from 1.170 percent.\par \par \uc2 Six-month rates <EURIBOR6MD=> inched up to 1.479 percent from 1.478 percent, longer-term 12-month rates <EURIBOR1YD=> climbed to 1.916 percent from 1.913 percent while shorter-term one-week rates <EURIBORSWD=> bucked the trend dipping to 0.781 percent from 0.784 percent.\par \par \uc2 EONIA overnight interest rates <EONIA> fixed lower at 0.700 percent on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 A recent decline in excess market liquidity is also keeping upward pressure on rates. Despite the ECB continuing to offer banks unlimited funding, it currently stands at just over 31 billion euros according to Reuters calculations.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  left euro zone interest rates on hold at a record low 1 percent this month but flagged plans to raise them next month, wrongfooting markets which until then had expected the first rise much later in the year.\par \par \uc2 The ECB also left all its liquidity \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  at full allotment for at least another three months, putting its 'exit strategy' from stimulus measures on hold for the second quarter running.\par \par \uc2 It is already back to its pre-crisis range of funding. Three-month loans are once again the longest maturity on offer and banks have now paid back all the six-month and 12-month loans the ECB injected during the turmoil. <^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\par \par \uc2 For graphic of EONIA trading volumes click {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://graphics.thomsonreuters.com/F/08/EZ_EONIA0810.gif"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://graphics.thomsonreuters.com/F/08/EZ_EONIA0810.gif}}}\par \par \uc2 For graphic of euro zone liquidity levels click\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://r.reuters.com/wer86p"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://r.reuters.com/wer86p}}}\uc2  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^>\par \par \uc2 Euribor rates are fixed daily by the Banking Federation of the European Union (FBE) shortly after 1000 GMT.\par \par \uc2 * For a table of the latest Euribor fixings for terms of one week to one year, double click on <EURIBOR=>\par \par \uc2 * For a table of the previous day's fixings of EONIA swap rates, which show market expectations for future overnight lending rates, double click on <EONIAINDEX>\par \par \uc2 * For graphs of historic Euribor and EONIA swap rates, right click on the links in angle brackets below, and select 'Related Graph'\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1 week    <EURIBORSWD=>    <EONIAINDEXSW=>\par 2 week    <EURIBOR2WD=>    <EONIAINDEX2W=>\par 3 week    <EURIBOR3WD=>    <EONIAINDEX3W=>\par 1 month   <EURIBOR1MD=>    <EONIAINDEX1M=>\par 2 month   <EURIBOR2MD=>    <EONIAINDEX2M=>\par 3 month   <EURIBOR3MD=>    <EONIAINDEX3M=>\par 4 month   <EURIBOR4MD=>    <EONIAINDEX4M=>\par 5 month   <EURIBOR5MD=>    <EONIAINDEX5M=>\par 6 month   <EURIBOR6MD=>    <EONIAINDEX6M=>\par 7 month   <EURIBOR7MD=>    <EONIAINDEX7M=>\par 8 month   <EURIBORS8M=>    <EONIAINDEX8M=>\par 9 month   <EURIBOR9MD=>    <EONIAINDEX9M=>\par 10 month  <EURIBOR10MD=>   <EONIAINDEX10M=>\par 11 month  <EURIBOR11MD=>   <EONIAINDEX11M=>\par 1 year    <EURIBOR1YD=>    <EONIAINDEX1Y=>\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Reporting by Frankfurt newsroom; Editing by John Stonestreet)\f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-EURIBOR/ (URGENT)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110318e73i000no\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
