\par\par \b \uc2 FACTBOX-How ECB  \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention \highlight\uc2  works\b0\par\par\uc2 617 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 11:34\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 FRANKFURT, March 18 (Reuters) - The European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  alongside \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the United States, the United Kingdom and others to calm volatile \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets in the wake of Japan's catastrophic earthquake, tsunami and nuclear disasters. [ID:nWEA9460]\par \par \uc2 Below is a factbox on how ECB \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  work and details of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's previous \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 HOW IT \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENES\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * The ECB can \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets without prior authority from euro zone or EU finance ministers. It can conduct sales or purchases of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  itself, or instruct national central banks that manage ECB reserves to conduct transactions on its behalf, or ask the same of foreign central banks with which it holds accounts.\par \par \uc2 * The ECB also can instruct the national central banks to transfer their own \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  assets to the ECB, in exchange for an interest-bearing claim. This would increase the ECB's fire power about four-fold, but it has never used this authority.\par \par \uc2 * The ECB can fund \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  not only with its reserves but by other means, such as \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps, and swaps with other central banks.\par \par \uc2 * The ECB can fire its biggest cannon by coordinating its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  with other major central banks.\par \par \uc2 In September 2000, it initiated a plan where the U.S. Federal Reserve and Bank of Japan joined it in buying euros to stem the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's sharp slide.\par \par \uc2 The action was followed by three waves of unilateral ECB \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in November and succeeded in putting a floor under the euro at 82 cents. There had been no \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  since until Friday's move.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  POWERS\par \par \uc2 * The European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  must conduct its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  within the framework of its primary objective, maintaining price stability. This means that if changes in the euro's value threaten inflationary or deflationary pressures, the ECB can \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets if price stability is at risk.\par \par \uc2 * European Union finance ministers have the authority to reach agreements on an exchange rate system for the euro, and can give general directions for exchange rate policy. The ECB can provide them with advice on these matters. The European Council of EU leaders agreed that it would exercise these powers in exceptional circumstances and without threatening the independence of the Eurosystem -- the ECB and national central banks.\par \par \uc2 In practice, EU finance ministers have never used these powers, leaving decisions on the euro and exchange rate policy up to the ECB.\par \par \uc2 * The ECB has a strong incentive to consult with finance ministers and keep them abreast of its thinking and any \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy plans, because ministers have the authority to give \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  direction. The monthly Eurogroup meeting of euro zone finance ministers and the ECB president is the usual forum for these discussions.\par \par \uc2 See also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.ecb.int/ecb/orga/tasks/html/foreign-exchange.en.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.ecb.int/ecb/orga/tasks/html/\b  \highlight22foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight22 .en.html}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  RESERVES\par \par \uc2 * There was a total of 185 billion euros in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves in the European System of Central Banks (ESCB) as of the end of last week. ECB does not specify \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  composition of its reserves, but traditionally they are held substantially in dollars.\par \par \uc2 * National central banks are required to contribute to the ECB reserves when they join the Eurosystem, based on a formula.\par \par \uc2 * The ECB manages its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to generate some income but it keeps them in highly liquid instruments. Some of the reserves are managed on its behalf by the national central banks. The ECB also has reserve accounts with other central banks, such as the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the Federal Reserve.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Marc Jones)\par \par \uc2 ECB/\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (FACTBOX)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110318e73i000nl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
