\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Rouble firms vs dollar on yen  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 614 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 09:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Up 0.9 percent against dollar\par \par \uc2 * Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , G7 decision benefit\par \par \uc2 * Strong oil, taxes to keep rouble firm for now\par \par \uc2 (Adds detail, closing prices)\par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, March 18 (Reuters) - The rouble recovered most of this week's losses against the dollar on Friday, tracking a rise in other emerging \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  after G7 central banks \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb the Japanese yen, improving global market sentiment.\par \par \uc2 Friday's recovery was enough for the rouble to collect nearly 1 percent in gains on the week against the dollar, with the Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  closing at 28.48 <RUBUTSTN=MCX>, up from 28.74 a week earlier.\par \par \uc2 Emerging market and commodity-driven \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  like the rouble have had a jittery week, with the threat of a nuclear disaster in earthquake-stricken Japan making investors less willing to hold higher-yielding but riskier assets.\par \par \uc2 But oil -- Russia's chief export -- remained strong, despite falling on Friday <CLc1> after Libyan leader Muammar Gaddafi's government said it would halt military action in response to a U.N. resolution for an immediate ceasefire [ID:nL3E7EI0B3.]\par \par \uc2 Crude prices are still more than 30 percent above the average of $75 a barrel assumed in Russia's 2011 budget.\par \par \uc2 "Additionally, the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , through its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , calmed the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, which can also benefit the rouble," dealer Sergei Fishgoit of Otkritiye said.\par \par \uc2 The Bank of Japan added a further 3 trillion yen ($38.01 billion) to money markets on Friday to shore up confidence in light of last week's devastating earthquake and tsunami and the unfolding nuclear crisis.\par \par \uc2 Finance ministers from the Group of Seven rich nations also agreed, in the first decision of its kind since 2000, to curb the yen's recent strength after the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  soared to an all-time high versus the dollar. [ID:nL3E7EH3HP]\par \par \uc2 "The rouble is likely to firm in the short-term, but the dynamics should be calmer," a dealer at a large foreign bank in Moscow said.\par \par \uc2 "Most likely, it will show significant growth against the dollar, where, judging from the developments on \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, there are strong weakening tendencies of the dollar."\par \par \uc2 The rouble lost substantially against the broadly strengthening European single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , closing the week down 1.7 percent at 40.27 <EURRUBTN=MCX>.\par \par \uc2 As a result, the Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  also slid against the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dollar-euro basket, closing at 33.78 <RUS=MCX>. some 0.4 percent weaker than last Friday.\par \par \uc2 If the weekend brings no major developments that could shake global markets, the rouble is seen firming further against the dollar and rebounding versus the basket, traders said.\par \par \uc2 The market will be closely watching the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision, due next week, on whether to further tighten monetary policy to curb inflation which doubled in the latest week. [ID:nLDE72F1MD]\par \par \uc2 Data on Friday showed the Russian economy performed slightly better last month than in February, bringing some comfort to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  [ID:nLDE72H1DR].\par \par \uc2 The regulator has been juggling the task of curbing inflation by tightening monetary policy while also shoring up economic growth.\par \par \uc2 But strong oil prices and monthly tax payments, which raise demand for rouble liquidity as exporters convert their revenues, give market players reasons to remain optimistic on the rouble.\par \par \uc2 "We think it is a good time to take advantage of temporary risk aversion in the market, due to the nuclear crisis in Japan, by opening long rouble positions at these levels," Anton Nikitin, an analyst at Renaissance Capital in Moscow, wrote in a note.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Vladimir Abramov; Writing by Lidia Kelly; Editing by Catherine Evans)\par \par \uc2 RUSSIA/ROUBLE (UPDATE 1)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110318e73i000hv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
