\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 747 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 03:07\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: G-7 PLEDGES RARE JOINT \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  AS CRISIS-STRICKEN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  SELLS YEN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Group of Seven industrial powers pledged to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets for the first time in a decade as Japan dumped yen on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets Friday to keep the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's record surge from further damaging an economy ravaged by earthquake, tsunami and nuclear disaster. (published 0204 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BERNANKE, TRICHET FIRST AMONG G-7 CENTRAL BANKERS SAYING WOULD HELP IN YEN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  -SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Joint \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets to curb the value of the yen was unanimously backed by all members of the Group of Seven industrialized nations, with U.S. Federal Reserve Chairman Ben Bernanke and European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  President Jean-Claude Trichet the first in expressing their support for the coordinated move, a G-7 official told Dow Jones Newswires. (published 0206 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par STATEMENT OF G-7 FINANCE MINISTERS AND \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  GOVERNORS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 We, the G-7 Finance Ministers and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Governors, discussed the recent dramatic events in Japan and were briefed by our Japanese colleagues on the current situation and the economic and financial response put in place by the authorities. (published 0146 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par WORLD \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : DOLLAR SURGES AGAINST YEN AS \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MOF \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENES\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 The U.S. dollar surged against the yen after the Group of Seven finance ministers agreed to joint \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to weaken the yen, as \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  struggles with multiple natural disasters and an ongoing nuclear emergency. (published 0110 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN FINANCE MINISTER: DOLLAR FALL TO AROUND Y76 WAS TAKEN INTO CONSIDERATION ON \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese Finance Minister Yoshihiko Noda said Friday that the dollar's plunge to its all-time low around the Y76 level was a factor taken into account in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's decision to seek cooperation in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets from its Group of Seven counterparts. (published 0200 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN YOSANO: G-7 MOVE MEANS IMPORTANCE OF YEN STABILITY WIDELY RECOGNIZED - NIKKEI \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's Economy Minister Kaoru Yosano Friday said the decision by the Group of Seven to conduct joint \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to curb the yen's strength means there is a common understanding of the importance of a stable Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the Nikkei reported. (published 0135 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: BOJ SHIRAKAWA: BOJ TO CONTINUE TO PROVIDE AMPLE LIQUIDITY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan Gov. Masaaki Shirakawa said Friday the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will continue to pump cash into Japan's financial system as needed to stabilize domestic financial markets as Japan and its Group of Seven counterparts act jointly to stabilize \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rates. (published 0107 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par SOURCE: BOJ WILL KEEP EASY CONDITIONS DURING \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  "will keep providing ample liquidity, along with yen funds injected via \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," a person familiar with the bank's thinking told Dow Jones Newswires Friday, suggesting that the bank is likely to leave the coordinated \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  unsterilized. (published 0112 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  GOVERNMENT PLANS TO ISSUE OVER Y10 TLN IN EARTHQUAKE RECONSTRUCTION BONDS -REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Japanese government is planning to issue more than Y10 trillion in earthquake reconstruction bonds to be bought in full directly by the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the Sankei Newspaper reported Friday citing government sources. (published 0012 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par WSJ: EBA: EU STRESS TESTS WILL FOCUS ON BANKS' CORE TIER 1 CAPITAL LEVELS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 European officials unveiled some details of the "stress tests" they plan to run on the continent's banks, hoping to show that the exercise will be tough enough to defuse fears about the sector's health. (published 0001 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par WSJ: BEHIND YEN'S RECORD SURGE; INDIVIDUAL INVESTORS, HEDGE FUNDS SCRAMBLED TO BUY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A day after a heart-stopping rally drove the Japanese yen to one of its sharpest ascents in history, traders and bankers blamed a freak onslaught of forced buying by Japanese individual investors and hedge funds--a barrage that came at the exact time of day when the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market is at its most vulnerable. (published 2326 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par US STOCK FUNDS INVESTING IN JAPAN HAD WEEKLY INFLOW OF $956M - LIPPER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. stock funds investing in Japan had $955.9 million in net inflows for the week ended March Wednesday, said Lipper. (published 2247 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par DATA SNAP: UK CONSUMER CONFIDENCE CONTINUES TO EVAPORATE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.K. consumers became even more pessimistic about the outlook for the economy and their job prospects during February, and less willing to spend, according to a monthly survey commissioned by the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Nationwide Building Society\f28 \uc2 \f2 . (published 0001 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 18-03-11 0207GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110318e73i0005j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
