\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 528 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 02:07\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par G-7 WILL \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  WITH \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  IN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREIGN EXCHANGE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MARKET - G-7 STATEMENT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Group of Seven finance ministers and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governors Friday expressed solidarity with \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and pledged to jointly \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market to ensure orderly markets. (published 0036 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  FINANCE MINISTER: G-7 AGREED ON JOINT \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's finance minister said Friday he secured a pledge from his Group of Seven counterparts to conduct joint \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to counter a sharp rise in the yen following last week's massive earthquake. (published 0028 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BOJ SHIRAKAWA: BOJ TO CONTINUE TO PROVIDE AMPLE LIQUIDITY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan Gov. Masaaki Shirakawa said Friday the bank will keep providing ample liquidity to the banking system to stabilize financial markets amid high concerns about the impact of the earthquake in Japan. (published 0017 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN GOVERNMENT PLANS TO ISSUE OVER Y10 TLN IN EARTHQUAKE RECONSTRUCTION BONDS -REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Japanese government is planning to issue more than Y10 trillion in earthquake reconstruction bonds to be bought in full directly by the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the Sankei Newspaper reported Friday citing government sources. (published 0012 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par WSJ: EBA: EU STRESS TESTS WILL FOCUS ON BANKS' CORE TIER 1 CAPITAL LEVELS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 European officials unveiled some details of the "stress tests" they plan to run on the continent's banks, hoping to show that the exercise will be tough enough to defuse fears about the sector's health. (published 0001 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par WSJ: BEHIND YEN'S RECORD SURGE; INDIVIDUAL INVESTORS, HEDGE FUNDS SCRAMBLED TO BUY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A day after a heart-stopping rally drove the Japanese yen to one of its sharpest ascents in history, traders and bankers blamed a freak onslaught of forced buying by Japanese individual investors and hedge funds--a barrage that came at the exact time of day when the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market is at its most vulnerable. (published 2326 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par US STOCK FUNDS INVESTING IN JAPAN HAD WEEKLY INFLOW OF $956M - LIPPER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. stock funds investing in Japan had $955.9 million in net inflows for the week ended March Wednesday, said Lipper. (published 2247 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par DATA SNAP: UK CONSUMER CONFIDENCE CONTINUES TO EVAPORATE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.K. consumers became even more pessimistic about the outlook for the economy and their job prospects during February, and less willing to spend, according to a monthly survey commissioned by the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Nationwide Building Society\f28 \uc2 \f2 . (published 0001 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BRAZIL TOMBINI: JAPAN CRISIS MAY AFFECT GLOBAL, LOCAL ECONOMY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The natural and nuclear disasters that struck Japan will introduce greater uncertainty to the global economy and could have an important influence on Brazil's economic policies, Brazilian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  President Alexandre Tombini said Thursday. (published 2303 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par  \par UPDATE: CHILE \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  SURPRISES WITH 50BPS RATE INCREASE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Chile\f28 \uc2 \f2  surprised markets Thursday evening and picked up the pace of its interest rate increases. (published 2241 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par MOODY'S DOWNGRADES ANOTHER $5.2 BILLION OF SUBPRIME RMBS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Moody's Investors Service downgraded a $5.2 billion batch of subprime residential mortgage-backed securities, as the agency continues to lower its expectations on underlying loans. (published 2245 GMT) [ 18-03-11 0107GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110318e73i00036\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
