\par\par \b \uc2 AT A GLANCE: Japan Nuclear Situation Hasn't Deteriorated, Remains Serious\b0\par\par\uc2 1,400 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 19:49\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    THE NEWS: \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan continued to battle the risk of radiation at the Fukushima Daiichi nuclear power plant Thursday, drenching the reactors with water cannons and seawater dropped by helicopters in a bid to cool the still-overheated reactors. Markets, in general, are pausing after three days of risk aversion stemming from the crisis.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par   NUCLEAR PLANT STATUS: \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Fukushima situation hasn't gotten worse in the past 24 hours, but it remains very serious, the International Atomic Energy Agency said Thursday. After a long delay because of high radiation levels, water cannon cooling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  commenced.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Efforts during the day to link the stricken plant to the main electricity grid appeared to have been unsuccessful. Bringing the reactor cooling functions on line could mark a turning point in controlling the situation.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par   QUESTIONS ABOUT REACTORS: \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Meanwhile, the U.S.-made reactors at Fukushima are coming under close scrutiny as experts point to flaws in their original design and the lack of a safety feature that the nuclear industry is only now starting to address.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par   THE HUMAN TOLL: \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The official death toll from the earthquake/tsunami was at 12,920, but almost everyone agrees it is likely to go much higher. For the survivors, government officials and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Tokyo Electric Power Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . warned of possible further power blackouts.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par   EXODUS WITHIN JAPAN: \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 As radiation worries grow, multinational companies and countries have stepped up efforts to move personnel away from the danger.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The U.K. has advised its citizens to consider leaving Tokyo and north of Tokyo, after days of trying to calm British nerves.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Companies as varied as \f28 \uc2 \f2 France Telecom\f28 \uc2 \f2  (FTE, FTE.FR) and fashion retailer \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hennes & Mauritz\f28 \uc2 \f2  (HM-B.SK) have either evacuated personnel or moved them south and west in Japan. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Google\f28 \uc2 \f2  maintains its policy since the start of the crisis: supporting employee decisions whether or not to stay.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par   SUPPLY CHAIN IMPACT: \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Even though Japan has the world's third-largest economy, the Japanese crisis will likely cause "pinch points in various supply chains," but is not likely to be "significant overall" to global trade, said \f28 \uc2 \f2 Fred Smith\f28 \uc2 \f2 , the chief executive of freight shipping company \f28 \uc2 \f2 FedEx Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . (FDX).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    KEY EVENT ON TAP: \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 G-7 nations will hold a teleconference at 6:00 p.m. EDT/2200 GMT to discuss the effects of the crisis. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is likely seen seeking approval for a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . Officially, the G-7 is expected to issue a statement of solidarity.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    JAPAN MOF 'PREPARED FOR BATTLE' ON YEN - SOURCE: \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's Finance Ministry is being increasingly vigilant against the yen's rise ahead of the G-7 teleconference, amid threats of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to weaken the yen.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The ministry is "prepared for battle" after the yen jumped to a record high in late U.S. trade Wednesday, with the dollar falling to Y76.25, a person familiar with the matter said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    MARKETS: \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - The dollar moved higher, but remains down against the yen on the day, after a source said the G-7 might support \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - Nymex crude futures moved back above $100 a barrel as Japan fears abated.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - Treasurys are down after enjoying three days of safe-haven flows.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - N.Y. stocks are higher after losing 3.6% over the previous three sessions.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones Newswires' coverage of the event and related news can be found by searching the code R/JA.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    LATEST STORIES: \par  \par G-7 FINANCE CHIEFS TO SUPPORT \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN FOREX INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  - NIKKEI \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Group of Seven finance ministers and central bankers are expected, in an emergency teleconference, to approve \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by Japanese monetary authorities to combat excessive yen strength, the Nikkei reported in its Friday morning edition. (published 1313 EDT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par WSJ UPDATE: HOW G-7 OFFICIALS MIGHT VIEW YEN IN CALL TODAY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 G-7 finance ministers will have three options on the table for the Japanese yen when they confer later today about the devastating earthquake and nuclear crisis rocking the world's third-largest economy: Say nothing, speak out against market volatility, or \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to stop it. (published 1245 EDT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par WSJ: FOREIGNERS RELOCATED WITHIN OR OUTSIDE STRICKEN JAPAN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Multinational companies stepped up efforts to move staff out of Japan, as worries about damaged nuclear reactors in the country grew.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par WSJ: FEDEX:JAPAN TRAGEDY MAY CAUSE CRIMPS IN WORLD SUPPLY CHAIN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The tragedy in Japan is likely to cause "pinch points in various supply chains" but is not likely to be "significant overall" to global trade, said \f28 \uc2 \f2 Fred Smith\f28 \uc2 \f2 , the chief executive of freight shipping company \f28 \uc2 \f2 FedEx Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . (FDX). He added despite the addition of higher fuel prices and unrest in the Middle East, the "dynamics of global trade" appear solid.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par IMF: JAPAN HAS NOT ASKED FOR FUND FINANCIAL ASSISTANCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan has not requested any financial assistance from the International Monetary Fund and Tokyo has the resources it needs to handle the current crisis, a fund spokeswoman said. (published 1245 EDT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN METI: MASSIVE TOKYO BLACKOUT MAY BE AVOIDED UNDER CURRENT DEMAND LEVEL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's trade ministry said the greater Tokyo area--the nation's crucial economic center--will likely avert a major blackout for the rest of the day, as the use of electricity has fallen since the morning after the government called on the public to save power. (published 0733 EDT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par DOLLAR MOVES HIGHER VS YEN ON REPOT G-7 WILL SUPPORT \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar moved higher against the yen, but still remained down on the day, after a report said leaders of the world's largest economies will support \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  into \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MOF 'READY FOR BATTLE' ON YEN - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's Finance Ministry is being increasingly vigilant against the yen's rise ahead of a teleconference among Group of Seven finance ministers, amid threats of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to weaken the yen. (published 1145 EDT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par WSJ: \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TAXPAYERS SEEN PAYING DAMAGES FROM NUCLEAR REACTORS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Once the crisis at Japan's crippled nuclear reactors ends and the time comes to allocate financial responsibility, there is likely to be only one party holding the bag: the Japanese taxpayer. (published 1527 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par US NUCLEAR INDUSTRY QUESTIONS 'SCIENTIFIC BASIS' OF US' 50-MILE EVACUATION IN JAPAN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The U.S. nuclear power industry is questioning the "scientific basis" of the Obama administration's decision to evacuate U.S. citizens and military personnel within a 50-mile radius from the Fukushima power plant in Japan. (published 1606 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par COMMODITIES RISE AS FEARS MODERATE OVER JAPAN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Commodities markets pushed higher as traders grew more confident in Japan's ability to recover from the earthquake and tsunami that ravaged the country. (published 1147 EDT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INTERVIEW: JAPAN QUAKE TO HIT URANIUM SHIPMENTS IN SHORT TERM - CANADA PREMIER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Canada's Saskatchewan province, the world's largest exporter of uranium, expects overseas shipments of the mineral to take a hit following radiation concerns at nuclear reactors in Japan after Friday's earthquake and tsunami. (published 1110 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: BOJ OFFERS ADDITIONAL Y5 TLN IMMEDIATE FUNDS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Japan announced the provision of emergency funds for a fourth straight day, continuing its effort to calm concern about the impact of the earthquake, tsunami and nuclear power crises on the economy. (published 2301 EDT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN REFINERY RUNS RECOVER; EXTERNAL SUPPLIES BEING LINED UP \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's refining sector is gradually restoring \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  following Friday's earthquake, but even by the end of the month refinery throughput is expected to remain well below pre-quake levels. (published 0708 EDT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par IAEA WARNED JAPAN OVER NUCLEAR QUAKE RISK, WIKILEAKS DOCUMENTS SHOW \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The International Atomic Energy Agency warned Japan two years ago that a strong earthquake could pose a "serious problem" for its nuclear power stations, the U.K. newspaper, The Daily Telegraph reported. (published 2150 EDT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BANK OF JAPAN'S RESPONSE TO CRISES UNPRECEDENTED -HKMA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Japan's response to the many disasters now befalling that country has already been unprecedented, Norman Chan, chief executive of the Hong Kong \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said. (published 0047 EDT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par EUROPEAN NUCLEAR DEBATE RAGES ON AS GERMAN OPPOSITION SHARPENS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Utility executives and a top nuclear official have robustly defended the nuclear industry in an intensifying debate over the suitability of atomic energy as a major energy source, as Germany signalled its determination to accelerate its transition away from nuclear power and toward renewables. (published 1306 EDT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - By Kerry Benn, Dow Jones Newswires, 212-416-2353 [ 17-03-11 1849GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110317e73h001g9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pn