\par\par \b \uc2 Coordinated  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Against Yen Strength Possible; G-7 Call Awaited\b0\par\par\uc2 763 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 19:30\par \uc2 Dow Jones Energy Service\par \uc2 NRG\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 - Market players stand guard for signs of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 - Thursday evening phone call could give clues on possible G-7 coordination.\par \par \uc2 - Japan might go it alone first, then ask for help.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Bradley Davis \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--An all-out coordinated assault on yen strength could be in the works, with the Group of Seven industrialized economies possibly agreeing to band together to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets in a conference call set to start around 2200 GMT Thursday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Whether Japan goes it alone, or whether it requests the firepower of its major-economy peers, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to stem yen strength is a foregone conclusion, many strategists and money managers said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The speed of the move," which saw the dollar Wednesday, in extremely volatile trading, plummet against the yen after breaching its all-time low, "was panic, not fundamentally based," said Thanos Papasavvas, head of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  management in London for \f28 \uc2 \f2 Investec Asset Management\f28 \uc2 \f2 , which has $70 billion in assets under management.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "That merits policy makers to come in and normalize events," he said. "Given the situation in Japan, the last thing they'd want is a spiraling" \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's economy has sagged for years under the weight of deflation; the last thing it needs, as it struggles to recover from the massive earthquake--and still deal with failing nuclear power plants--is a strong \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which make its exports more expensive, analysts said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Given the volatile, disorderly moves in the yen, the G-7 leaders could decide to coordinate \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to assist \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as "a last resort," said Geoffrey Yu, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at \f28 \uc2 \f2 UBS\f28 \uc2 \f2  in London.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The last time central banks acted together in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets was in 2000 to boost the euro, which suffered a crisis of confidence; they also worked in concert in 2008 to slash interest rates in response to the financial crisis, Yu noted.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Based on those past events, the central banks that would join the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in a coordinated \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would likely be the Federal Reserve, the European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Canada\f28 \uc2 \f2 , the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Swiss National Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  and the Bank of England, Yu said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Joint \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will involve selling of Japanese yen in markets--and the amounts would have to at least match what the BOJ would be able to do on its own, Yu said. "The signalling effect would be far more important to markets--to the Japanese exporters its 'We're here to help,' and to the rest of the market it's, 'Know what you are up against.'"\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese exporters are under pressure from the record strength of the yen. Speculators and other \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market participants are wary of the sharp reversals in the market and potential losses that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  can cause.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A person close to the situation told Dow Jones Newswires on Thursday that the Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stood ready to act; the MOF instructs the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to sell yen in the event of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Even if global central banks eventually join \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to depress the yen, Japan is likely to fire the first shot, Investec's Papasavvas said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Last September, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's yen-selling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  totalled Y2 trillion.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will likely wait until there's a brief spike higher in the dollar against the yen, then surprise markets with a flood of dollar purchases to add strong momentum to the move higher in the greenback, pushing it to around Y82 or Y83, he said. Thursday afternoon, the dollar traded at Y78.96 after having dropped to an all-time low of Y76.25 late Wednesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 If that doesn't work, "they may ask their friends to come in," calling on global central banks to help, Papasavvas said. "The issue is: They don't want to be there all alone, trying to stop this by themselves."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Scott Mather, Pimco's head of global bond portfolio management, said he would "seriously doubt" major central banks will \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in concert to push down the yen.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The G-7 talks, Mather said, could result in an implicit agreement among leading economies to not oppose \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which is typically sternly discouraged.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "For one of the main anchors of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  world to begin a new episode of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ...is probably not something that every country would like to fully endorse," Mather said. But "they may simply be able to excuse it and find reasons to justify it."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Bradley Davis, Dow Jones Newswires; 212-416-2654; bradley.davis@dowjones.com [ 03-17-11 1430ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument NRG0000020110317e73h00044\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
