\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: Buy Dong Energy A/S Bonds Amid Japan News-Jyske\b0\par\par\uc2 1,276 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 17:09\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par Markettalk.eu@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1609 GMT [Dow Jones] \f28 \uc2 \f2 Jyske Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  upgrades corporate bonds for privately-held Danish firm Dong Energy A/S. This comes in the wake of Japan's nuclear power crisis. The bank raises its recommendation on the Euro 5.5% 3005 issue to buy from hold and on the Euro 7.75% 3010 issue to strong buy from buy. Jyske says the effect of the crisis is likely to boost Japan's demand for natural gas. Jyske says redirection of supply from Europe to Japan is expected to reduce European excess capacity in natural gas and in turn lift gas prices. (katarina.gustafsson@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 1549 GMT [Dow Jones] The yield spread between Irish and German 2-year paper is 18 bps wider at 727 bps, according to Tradeweb prices, while other peripheral-Germany spreads are unchanged or tighter. However, traders note very wide bid-offer spreads in both Irish cash and CDS prices and an absence of trading activity. (mark.brown@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 11:47 (Dow Jones) The dollar/yen might be helped by the fact that the rate differential between US and Japanese 2-year rates are moving higher. "The US 2-year swap rate (0.79%) has crept back above its 200-day moving average, currently 0.7825%," says Robert Sinche at RBS Securities. "In this context, a simple relationship between the 2-year rate gap and USD/JPY suggests the potential - subject to headlines out of Japan - for USD/JPY to regain the psychologically-important 80 level on its own in the near term, the BOJ's preferred outcome." (javier.david@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 Call us at (212) 416-2354 or email patrick.sullivan@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 Visit the Market Talk blog at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.djnmarkettalk.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.djnmarkettalk.com}}}\par \par \uc2 1538 GMT [Dow Jones] Polish bond yields are higher after February data on industrial output in the country came in higher-than-expected, rekindling speculation that interest rates here might still be raised in April, a trader says. The market is likely to be steady on Friday with no data scheduled in Poland and some demand may appear if the zloty continues to strengthen, the trader says. Average yield on 2-year bonds is at 5.01% from 4.98% late Wednesday, 5-year at 5.79% from 5.76%, 10-year at 6.27% from 6.25%. EUR/PLN is at 4.0671 from 4.0988. (marcin.sobczyk@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1534 GMT [Dow Jones] Gilts are down, falling in line with bunds and Treasurys as investors book profits after the sharp gains made in recent sessions. Risky assets such as stocks are stronger having been pummeled in the last few days on fears over the nuclear crisis in Japan and tensions in the Middle East. "Equities and commodities are rising so that's taken some shine off bonds but it remains to be seen how long this lasts," says a strategist. Earlier Thursday, there was strong demand for a GBP2.75% billion auction of the new 10-year gilt. June gilts are down 0.57 at 118.28 and the 10-year gilt yield is up 6bps at 3.535%. (neelabh.chaturvedi@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 11:28(Dow Jones) \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  CDS spreads are one reason \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is necessary, says Hans Redeker, strategist with \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2 . One way to cut into "the risk premium on the CDS side is to weaken the Japanese yen," he says, adding it would also create more confidence for the economy as domestic demand remains under pressure. Japan's 5-year CDS spread is 6bp wider, from Wednesday, at 110bps, according to Markit. (erin.mccarthy@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 Call us at (212) 416-2354 or email patrick.sullivan@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 Visit the Market Talk blog at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.djnmarkettalk.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.djnmarkettalk.com}}}\par \par \uc2 1527 GMT [Dow Jones] The Monetary Policy Council of Poland's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to judge the monetary policy trend of the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and wait for more stability in global markets, before raising rates, says BRE. The MPC will pay more attention to lower-than-expected February CPI and wages and to Thursday's higher-than-expected industrial output data, when it decides on rates in early April, says BRE. February industrial output which came in at +10.7%, would have been a positive surprise for the MPC, which in its March minutes said it was uncertain about the pace of Poland's economic recovery, notes BRE. (marcin.sobczyk@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 11:18 (Dow Jones) Citing the recovery of credit card issuers, \uc2 Moody's\uc2  says its outlook for the U.S. credit card industry is stable. Delinquencies and charge-offs have been declining in recent quarters so the improvement trend is likely to continue, says Curt Beaudoin, author of the report. Asset quality has improved as employment fundamentals are better and issuers have charged off bad loans and replaced them with new loans with tighter lending standards. Lending criteria remain high, as well. (anusha.shrivastava@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 Call us at (212) 416-2354 or email patrick.sullivan@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 Visit the Market Talk blog at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.djnmarkettalk.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.djnmarkettalk.com}}}\par \par \uc2 1515 GMT [Dow Jones] Bunds started the day in negative territory and have continued to drift lower as stock markets rally, re-couping some of their recent losses. The June contract is 64 ticks lower at 123.01. Bunds are also under pressure from Thursday's Spanish and French multi-tranche bond auctions with in excess of EUR12.5 billion of paper sold. Apart from T-bills, no new paper is expected in Europe until next Wednesday. In the cash market the 2-year bund yields 1.535% and the 10-year 3.145%, flattening the curve by 2 bps to 161 bps. (nick.cawley@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1456 GMT [Dow Jones] Minutes of the March meeting of the Polish MPC show the council pays more attention to economic growth than to CPI in its policy decisions, says BPH economist Adam Antoniak. Notes the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's main goal is to ensure stability of prices. The MPC doesn't seem to have a firm opinion about the pace of economic growth and may delay monetary action until new macroeconomic data are released, Antoniak says. (marcin.sobczyk@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 10:45 (Dow Jones) Mexico's peso is recovering some of Wednesday's losses as stocks pick up on positive weekly U.S. jobs data. The dollar was recently quoted at MXN12.1115 in Mexico City, according to Infosel, compared with MXN12.1465 at the previous close. The peso's rebound is so far more cautious than the one seen earlier in the week, when it also had depreciated sharply in a single session on worries about the Japan crisis. Japan-related risk remains, and analysts see 12.20-12.21 as a key level to watch in the event of another selloff. (anthony.harrup@dowjones)\par \par \uc2 Call us at (212) 416-2354 or email patrick.sullivan@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 Visit the Market Talk blog at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.djnmarkettalk.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.djnmarkettalk.com}}}\par \par \uc2 10:41 (Dow Jones) Canadian dollar finds session highs against a broadly weaker U.S. dollar, rising along with equities and the Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's growth-linked peers. U.S. dollar is lower, at C$0.9838, from C$0.9909 late Wednesday, according to data provider CQG. (karen.johnson@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 Call us at (212) 416-2354 or email patrick.sullivan@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 Visit the Market Talk blog at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.djnmarkettalk.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.djnmarkettalk.com}}}\uc2  [ 03-17-11 1209ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020110317e73h000at\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
