b0 \highlight\uc2 's main goal is to ensure stability of prices. The MPC doesn't seem to have a firm opinion about the pace of economic growth and may delay monetary action until new macroeconomic data are released, Antoniak says. (marcin.sobczyk@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 10:45 (Dow Jones) Mexico's peso is recovering some of Wednesday's losses as stocks pick up on positive weekly U.S. jobs data. The dollar was recently quoted at MXN12.1115 in Mexico City, according to Infosel, compared with MXN12.1465 at the previous close. The peso's rebound is so far more cautious than the one seen earlier in the week, when it also had depreciated sharply in a single session on worries about the Japan crisis. Japan-related risk remains, and analysts see 12.20-12.21 as a key level to watch in the event of another selloff. (anthony.harrup@dowjones)\par \par \uc2 Call us at (212) 416-2354 or email patrick.sullivan@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 Visit the Market Talk blog at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.djnmarkettalk.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.djnmarkettalk.com}}}\par \par \uc2 10:41 (Dow Jones) Canadian dollar finds session highs against a broadly weaker U.S. dollar, rising along with equities and the Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's growth-linked peers. U.S. dollar is lower, at C$0.9838, from C$0.9909 late Wednesday, according to data provider CQG. (karen.johnson@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 Call us at (212) 416-2354 or email patrick.sullivan@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 Visit the Market Talk blog at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.djnmarkettalk.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.djnmarkettalk.com}}}\par \par \uc2 1435 GMT [Dow Jones] PLN is stronger after industrial output data, with the robust figure for February, +10.7%, adding fuel to monetary policy hawks, says \uc2 Bank Millennium\uc2 . Solid output should be read together with the below-expectations CPI figure for the month, +3.6%, and it's too early to say if rates will for sure go up 