\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: 2-year Spreads Might Push Yen Lower -RBS\b0\par\par\uc2 1,284 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 16:47\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 11:47 (Dow Jones) The dollar/yen might be helped by the fact that the rate differential between US and Japanese 2-year rates are moving higher. "The US 2-year swap rate (0.79%) has crept back above its 200-day moving average, currently 0.7825%," says Robert Sinche at RBS Securities. "In this context, a simple relationship between the 2-year rate gap and USD/JPY suggests the potential - subject to headlines out of Japan - for USD/JPY to regain the psychologically-important 80 level on its own in the near term, the BOJ's preferred outcome." (javier.david@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 Call us at (212) 416-2354 or email patrick.sullivan@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 Visit the Market Talk blog at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.djnmarkettalk.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.djnmarkettalk.com}}}\par \par \uc2 1538 GMT [Dow Jones] Polish bond yields are higher after February data on industrial output in the country came in higher-than-expected, rekindling speculation that interest rates here might still be raised in April, a trader says. The market is likely to be steady on Friday with no data scheduled in Poland and some demand may appear if the zloty continues to strengthen, the trader says. Average yield on 2-year bonds is at 5.01% from 4.98% late Wednesday, 5-year at 5.79% from 5.76%, 10-year at 6.27% from 6.25%. EUR/PLN is at 4.0671 from 4.0988. (marcin.sobczyk@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1534 GMT [Dow Jones] Gilts are down, falling in line with bunds and Treasurys as investors book profits after the sharp gains made in recent sessions. Risky assets such as stocks are stronger having been pummeled in the last few days on fears over the nuclear crisis in Japan and tensions in the 