ared with MXN12.1465 at the previous close. The peso's rebound is so far more cautious than the one seen earlier in the week, when it also had depreciated sharply in a single session on worries about the Japan crisis. Japan-related risk remains, and analysts see 12.20-12.21 as a key level to watch in the event of another selloff. (anthony.harrup@dowjones)\par \par \uc2 Call us at (212) 416-2354 or email patrick.sullivan@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 Visit the Market Talk blog at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.djnmarkettalk.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.djnmarkettalk.com}}}\par \par \uc2 10:41 (Dow Jones) Canadian dollar finds session highs against a broadly weaker U.S. dollar, rising along with equities and the Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's growth-linked peers. U.S. dollar is lower, at C$0.9838, from C$0.9909 late Wednesday, according to data provider CQG. (karen.johnson@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 Call us at (212) 416-2354 or email patrick.sullivan@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 Visit the Market Talk blog at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.djnmarkettalk.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.djnmarkettalk.com}}}\par \par \uc2 1435 GMT [Dow Jones] PLN is stronger after industrial output data, with the robust figure for February, +10.7%, adding fuel to monetary policy hawks, says \uc2 Bank Millennium\uc2 . Solid output should be read together with the below-expectations CPI figure for the month, +3.6%, and it's too early to say if rates will for sure go up in April, Millennium says. EUR/PLN is at 4.0753 from 4.0988 late Wednesday. (marcin.sobczyk@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1416 GMT [Dow Jones] \uc2 UBS\uc2  is sticking to its call for the SNB to raise interest rates in mid-June, based on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's assessment of the outlook for the Swiss economy, issued earlier Thursday. "Three factors could delay an increase in SNB rates - namely soft economic fundamentals, materially lower inflation data over the next three months, or a material CHF appreciation from current levels," according to economist Reto Huenerwadel. "All eyes will be on the ECB, and in a scenario where it hikes rates in April, we don't expect the SNB to lag in monetary tightening steps," he argues. (neil.maclucas@dowjones.com) [ 03-17-11 1147ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020110317e73h000am\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (japan near10 interven*) and (rst=trtw or rst=tprw or rst=tdjw) and (central bank or ministry of finance or treasury ministry or monetary authority)\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Datum\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 01/01/1995 bis 21/08/2023\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\row } \tr